            "step_id": "sel-noprac-01",
            "step_kind": "core",
            "lesson_objective_id": "sel-noprac-obj-1",
            "instructional_type": "explain_then_practise",
            "note": "Each digit has a value that depends on its position.\nIn 4 528, the 5 stands for 5 hundreds, the 2 stands for 2 tens and the 8 stands for 8 units.\nIn 70 316 the 7 stands for 70 000 and the 3 stands for 300.\nThe value of 9 in 9 041 is 9 000.",
            "blocks": [
              {
                "type": "explanation",
                "text": "Position decides value."
              }
            ],
            "activities": [
              {
                "who": "teacher",
                "what": "Explains the rule and works an example"
              },
              {
                "who": "student",
                "what": "Solves questions in their notes"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "step_id": "sel-noprac-02",
            "step_kind": "core",
            "lesson_objective_id": "sel-noprac-obj-2",
            "instructional_type": "explain_then_practise",
            "note": "To write a number in expanded form, split it by place value.\n4 528 = 4000 + 500 + 20 + 8.\n70 316 = 70000 + 300 + 10 + 6.\n9 041 = 9000 + 40 + 1.\nAdding them back gives the original number, so 4000 + 500 + 20 + 8 = 4528.",
            "blocks": [
              {
                "type": "worked_example",
                "text": "4 528 = 4000 + 500 + 20 + 8."
              }
            ],
            "activities": [
