            "step_id": "sel-drawn-01",
            "step_kind": "core",
            "lesson_objective_id": "sel-drawn-obj-1",
            "instructional_type": "explain_then_practise",
            "note": "A right angle measures 90 degrees.\nA straight angle measures 180 degrees and a full turn measures 360 degrees.\nAn acute angle is less than 90 degrees, so 35 degrees and 72 degrees are acute.\nAn obtuse angle is between 90 and 180 degrees, so 115 degrees is obtuse.\nTwo angles on a straight line add to 180, so if one is 55 the other is 125.\n\n**fig-01.** Two lines meeting at a right angle, with the square mark shown.\n\n\\begin{center}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}\n  \\draw (0,0) -- (3,0);\n  \\draw (0,0) -- (0,3);\n  \\draw (0,0.3) -- (0.3,0.3) -- (0.3,0);\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n\\end{center}",
            "blocks": [
              {
                "type": "explanation",
                "text": "A right angle is 90 degrees."
              }
            ],
